        "original_author_id": 0,
        "title": "RFE: make `tea repo ct` just an option to `tea repo create`",
        "body": "I think it is a horrible user interface design to hide something which is just an option (from the user point of view at least; it is probably much more complicated inside of the program, but user doesn’t care that much) behind a name which is completely impossible to remember. Yes, I know it should be `tea repo create --template NAME_OF_TEMPLATE` which has been taken, so either rename `--template` to `--make-template` or create new option `--use-template`, but either of these would be much more discoverable than completely different sub-command with a name which I just cannot remember.",
